{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/424557-wolf-amongst-sheep-playing-an-abyssal-posing-as-a-solar","id":424557,"title":"Wolf amongst sheep - playing an abyssal posing as a solar","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-01T15:04:08-08:00","id":424557,"title":"Wolf amongst sheep - playing an abyssal posing as a solar","content":"Hello guys.<br /> <br /> tl;dr : help me hide my chars abyssal nature.<br /> <br /> My group is gonna try our hand at Exalted.<br /> I've played 1st ed a bit, but this will be the first time I try 2nd edition, and none (including the ST) have played Exalted before. We will be playing solars... or rather THEY will.<br /> I was tossing around concepts and realised that one almost felt like an abyssal, and then I got the idea of playing as an abyssal, and soon after I found the Solar Impersonation Style charm.<br /> So in short I'm gonna print out a solar character sheet and write all my stuff on that.<br /> <br /> The story will start (and probably stay) in the west.<br /> My character idea so far is a day caste. Hulking, but suprisingly sly, and basicly a one man pirate riding a Folding ship (since my circle will need a boat).<br /> My deathlord will probably be the Boddisvata and I will come from one of his islands. Exactly what my mission will be, or how/if I ever gonna turn on my liege and try to be a hero, or if I will stay bad is not decided yet. We will have to see how things work out. The only thing I know is that the first adventure will be a mini-treasurehunt, but otherwise the ST is both tight lipped, and has not 100% decided yet. Probably help him create war between other countries and get people to hate/fear solar.<br /> <br /> Since I might have to turn &quot;mini boss&quot; if my party finds out my nature and try to kill me, I have to build a somewhat efficent killer.<br /> I will have high melee, and will be sporting the five point artifact sword Soul Mirror (since it's decent as is AND I can boost it and go boss mode).<br /> I will have kinda high sailing, since I will be our groups &quot;cab&quot;. My deathlord will provide me with the Folding ship.<br /> <br /> Now comes the part where I'm having trouble.<br /> How will I create a charcter able to hide in plain sight?<br /> <br /> I will of course get Solar Impersonation Style, 5 points in larceny and high manipulation.<br /> I will also spend points to get a hearthstone so I can regen essence even in creation.<br /> But otherwise? I don't even know what skill governs bluffchecks, nor what could make me get caught so I don't know how to build my character smartly.<br /> <br /> Here are some random thoughts:<br /> have atleast decent awarness so I can notice if someone (for instance: my circle) is spying on me?<br /> spirits, will they and their ability to be invisible, be a problem?<br /> get decent stealth?<br /> get a cheap item made from oricalcum, having it kinda like a meta-game bluff (the same as when I use a standard solar char. sheet)?<br /> other artefacts that can help with hiding my nature? Maybe Everyman Armour?<br /> My concept started out as a one man pirate and I don't wanna loose his badassery, so I'd get 8 points to spend on physical attributes, but otherwise I'm kinda open to suggestions.<br /> <br /> So that's kinda where I am.<br /> Hope y'all have some nice tips since I'm a wee bit lost about how to hide my nature best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4872-evilof","name":"evilof","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T15:47:07-08:00","id":424615,"title":"","content":"Lying is usually covered under manipulation.<br /> If you're considering an artifact just go with soulsteel for it. If it has an attunement cost then soulsteel costs less, and the rest of the players really shouldn't be checking your character sheet to tell how much your attuning your artifacts for anyway. In game you're a pirate call it loot from a previous raid and that you've gotten used to the fight it gives you. I doubt a soulsteel artifact will make you stand out too much and who knows if you do it well enough they might give you an orichalcum version of it if they ever find one. The other advantage being that attuning the &quot;offtype&quot; artifact will give you larger essence pool than actually attuning one. Whether you choose to just take advantage of the extra motes or use it as bluff so you can have an extra charm up your sleeve in an emergency is up to you.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't invest charm space into countering spirits, but if you play off the superstitious angle then you could justify having some counter measures against spirits around your quarters as a case of &quot;I have killed a lot of people and I don't need their ghosts coming after me.&quot; You're going for the one man pirate raid, so I actually wouldn't bother with stealth unless the failing is something that makes your character try and learn it. I would actually stick to becoming real good at fighting from multiple ranges. Like a sheath of throwing knives and ranks in throw so you can just knife people coming up on the other side of your ship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T16:05:00-08:00","id":424624,"title":"","content":"If you're going to be a Day then you already have a lot of the bases you want to cover, covered - Awareness, Larceny, and Stealth. <br /> <br /> It should not even be that big a deal to be more overt in your allegiance toward Skullstone - there's a canon Solar named Moray Darktide who is basically a privateer for Skullstone. That the rest of the players haven't played before should be a good method to telling them that the Deathlords don't need to be inherently evil (and really, shouldn't be but that's a whole other story). I mean, being a privateer for Skullstone comes across like a very reasonable &quot;real job,&quot; in the end.<br /> <br /> You're going to want to invest in a degree of combat and Dodge (it's Caste, may as well go for it). You might look into favoring Sail and a social ability to go with that Manipulation - I seem to recall Abyssal Presence and Socialize as being pretty good.<br /> <br /> Just keep in mind that a supposed party member who suddenly goes PVP on the rest might lead to bad feelings OOC. Talk it all over with your ST privately first - the ST definitely has to sign off on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T17:19:13-08:00","id":424690,"title":"","content":"Lying is manipulation+socialise.<br /> Solar Impersonation Style should cover your anima, hearthstones are vital, but you seem to have got that covered.<br /> Beyond that, the biggest problem is probably resonance.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T18:15:33-08:00","id":424725,"title":"","content":"Wolf among the hounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T00:24:22-08:00","id":424949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I will have high melee, and will be sporting the five point artifact sword Soul Mirror (since it's decent as is AND I can boost it and go boss mode). </div> </div> </div>An ST running second edition for the first time should probably disallow any 4-5 artifact at character creation as a general sanity preserving measure, additionally, I'm not certain the particulars of Solar imitation style would cover hiding the impacts of carrying around one the most obviously evil artifacts anyone could possess - having that thing doesn't necessarily reveal you as an Abyssal, but it's a giant neon sign screaming 'bad person!'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1j0RQNTrhSQVIjBJw3555qA1S9Hih1SRwychiPhEwm9k/pub\" target=\"_blank\">Whitescrub Tundra Project</a>: a fan-made setting reference for Exalted 3e.<br /> <a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/10769032/1/\" target=\"_blank\">Edge of Underleaves</a> A pair of dragon-blooded dare the jungles of the southwest.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4060-mechalich","name":"Mechalich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4060_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"133"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T08:39:35-08:00","id":425250,"title":"","content":"<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42\">nalak42</a>: thanks for the tips. Maybe I should check for a thaumaturgic protection or something similar for my cabin atleast, or get spiritdetecting glance (or the abyssal equal) to protect my secrets.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean\">Zelbinnean</a>: Yeah, I saw the solar working for the Boddisvata. I have to check with the ST about how hidden my background should be. I think he wants me like a spy amongst solars and to, atleast at first, not make my alligeance known.<br /> also, about going PVP? Already checked it with him and I think it will turn out fine. I, as a player and oft-times GM/ST, will aim for more a dramaticly correct battle. My goal won't be to win be luring one circle mate into a secluded meeting and going full nova to kill him/her, and doing the same to the rest or something similar.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz\">The Wizard of Oz</a>: resonance, and handling it, is gonna make it both challenging and FUN <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene\">hippokrene</a>: &quot;</b>Wolf among the hounds.&quot; might indeed be a better title :P<br /> <br /> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4060-mechalich\">Mechalich</a>: for 99% of the time it will &quot;just&quot; be a soulsteel grand daiklave with an extra fear-effect. Consuming the souls will only be used to boost as a last resort (aka if I've been made or if we are facing a total party kill). Mechanicly it's not THAT difficult to handle I feel like. I can talk to him about removing the abilities to hurt WP and cause fear and get maybe get something less fiddly. Like the ability to throw it and have it return or something.<br /> Also: yes, I will come of as a bad person, but I'm not gonna try to play a nice character anyways. Compassion One city here I come :P</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4872-evilof","name":"evilof","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T09:29:34-08:00","id":425322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/424557-wolf-amongst-sheep-playing-an-abyssal-posing-as-a-solar?p=424949#post424949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> having that thing doesn't necessarily reveal you as an Abyssal, but it's a giant neon sign screaming 'bad person!'</div> </div> </div> </div>How so? Jiunan Nightwarden has one, people seem to think he's an okay guy. I think Black Ice Shadow has a soulsteel weapon too, but I'm not sure about that.<br /> <br /> Most people don't know what the hell soulsteel even is. Those that do may or may not regard your willingly using it as making you a bad person or not.<br /> <br /> Now, MAKING soulsteel artifacts where people can see you, different story.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T09:35:13-08:00","id":425326,"title":"","content":"Yeah it would do a lot of good for the game to get rid of notions like &quot;wear orichalcum = obvious Anathema; wear soulsteel = obvious sociopath monster.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T09:47:47-08:00","id":425356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/424557-wolf-amongst-sheep-playing-an-abyssal-posing-as-a-solar?p=425326#post425326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah it would do a lot of good for the game to get rid of notions like &quot;wear orichalcum = obvious Anathema; wear soulsteel = obvious sociopath monster.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>True this.<br /> <br /> I mean... don't get me wrong, it would be perfectly reasonable in-setting for someone who knows what soulsteel is to regard anyone who is willingly attuned to and uses a soulsteel artifact as a terrible human being. That's a stance that is logically and ethically justifiable! But it is going to be far from the default and not a ton of people even know what soulsteel is.<br /> <br /> I've never gotten the whole &quot;you're wearing orichalcum, you're obviously an Anathema&quot; thing. A lot of people are just going to think you're festooned in gold; this clearly makes you a cut above normal folks but not, you know, a walking demon. Those who know what orichalcum actually is are likely to assume you're a Dragon-Blood if you make even a cursory effort at presenting that impression. If you're wearing orichalcum superheavy plate with an orichalcum grand daiklave... yeah, okay, at that point you had probably better stay out of any satrapies, but that's the most extreme case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T09:58:37-08:00","id":425368,"title":"","content":"I always played soulsteel artifacts as slightly unnerving to look at and it just made more sense if you knew how they were made. Like a soulsteel wavecutter diaklave is just going to cause people to be on edge when they can see it. I always had it as artifacts are not the easiest things on the planet to come by so people with the means and reasons to use them will just use what they can get. Like DBs have a strong preference for Jade artifacts, but if a wyld hunt yields a dead lunar with a moon silver bow and the DB was hoping to get an artifact bow he's taking the moonsilver.<br /> <br /> As far as hiding allegience to the Bodhisvatta if you really need to you can always say your character comes from that territory and has great respect for the teachings of the Silver Prince because that's how he was raised. (I forget if that was the cover's name, but the trick remains stable I think.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T10:56:48-08:00","id":425426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/424557-wolf-amongst-sheep-playing-an-abyssal-posing-as-a-solar?p=425368#post425368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as hiding allegience to the Bodhisvatta if you really need to you can always say your character comes from that territory and has great respect for the teachings of the Silver Prince because that's how he was raised. (I forget if that was the cover's name, but the trick remains stable I think.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm probably gonna be open about coming from those islands as a sailor on the boats that ship zombies around to scurry the ocean floor, and thats how I came by the sword.<br /> I might try to work it into reverence for the dead (good for roleplaying) and maybe wearing things related to death (so as not to have the -2 penalty). Maybe get a great billowing cloak made from a funeraray shroud or some such.<br /> <br /> Also: yes, he goes by the Silver Prince now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4872-evilof","name":"evilof","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T12:41:38-08:00","id":425546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/424557-wolf-amongst-sheep-playing-an-abyssal-posing-as-a-solar?p=425356#post425356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean... don't get me wrong, it would be perfectly reasonable in-setting for someone who knows what soulsteel is to regard anyone who is willingly attuned to and uses a soulsteel artifact as a terrible human being.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? It's not like I <i>made</i> it. I'm just <i>using</i> it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's a stance that is logically and ethically justifiable! </div> </div> </div><i>Is</i> it? That a thousand souls were imprisoned to <i>make</i> the blade is regrettable, but once they're imprisoned, they're imprisoned - wielding the sword is no more a moral crime than wielding a jade daiklave. It's not like leaving it where you found it will hasten the ghosts to their final rest.<br /> <br /> (Soul Mirror's a different story specifically because it steals and consumes the souls of those it kills, but we're just talking regular soulsteel here.)<br /> <br /> If you're one of those &quot;moral&quot; vegetarians, I can understand why you may avoid <i>killing</i> an animal for the purpose of eating it, even when you're starving, but that's not what this is: it's coming across an animal that's already dead, and saying that <i>not dying</i> would be the morally wrong thing to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-02-2015, 03:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T12:51:58-08:00","id":425559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/424557-wolf-amongst-sheep-playing-an-abyssal-posing-as-a-solar?p=425546#post425546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but once they're imprisoned, they're imprisoned</div> </div> </div> </div>Until you throw the Soulsteel into Oblivion. If you get the chance. But yes, might as well put it to good use until then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T12:58:06-08:00","id":425577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusk Shine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/424557-wolf-amongst-sheep-playing-an-abyssal-posing-as-a-solar?p=425559#post425559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Until you throw the Soulsteel into Oblivion.</div> </div> </div> </div>But then <i>you're</i> the one <i>destroying souls</i>.<br /> That's like going to a maximum-security prison and murdering all the death-row inmates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T13:18:35-08:00","id":425602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/424557-wolf-amongst-sheep-playing-an-abyssal-posing-as-a-solar?p=425577#post425577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then <i>you're</i> the one <i>destroying souls</i>.<br /> That's like going to a maximum-security prison and murdering all the death-row inmates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that Soulsteel is described as ocassionaly moaning and stuff, I'd guess being in it isn't exactly &quot;comfortable&quot;. So no, I'm not murdering death row inmates who are sitting in clean cells and are in perfect health. I'm euthanising torture victims which I can't save. The alternative is subjecting them to eternal torture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T08:45:32-08:00","id":426602,"title":"","content":"There is probably some way to invent a spell or some such to release soulsteel victims from the metal and back into circulation.<br /> Step 1. Invent spell<br /> Step 2. Steal all the ships the Boddisvata has created<br /> Step 3. Release all the souls<br /> Step 4. Rejoice at being the ultimate good guy<br /> Step 5. Get killed by the Boddisvata and regret your lifes choices.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4872-evilof","name":"evilof","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T09:13:49-08:00","id":426625,"title":"","content":"Obligatory &quot;3rd edition is just about to come out, if you didn't know&quot; post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1414-pyrosorc","name":"Pyrosorc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T09:29:20-08:00","id":426633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pyrosorc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/424557-wolf-amongst-sheep-playing-an-abyssal-posing-as-a-solar?p=426625#post426625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obligatory &quot;3rd edition is just about to come out, if you didn't know&quot; post.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's <i>that</i> got to do with the morality of using soulsteel? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:White\">Doubting the relevance, since both Abyssals and Exigents-that-can-be-mocked-up-into-Abyssals are like a year away; either the OP's group doesn't ditch his PC for the sake of Ex3, in which case the proximity of Ex3 (and thus your post) is irrelevant, <b>or</b> the OP's group ditches his PC for the sake of Ex3, in which case this whole thread (and thus your post) is irrelevant.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-03-2015, 12:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T09:39:47-08:00","id":426637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evilof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/424557-wolf-amongst-sheep-playing-an-abyssal-posing-as-a-solar#post424557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since I might have to turn &quot;mini boss&quot; if my party finds out my nature and try to kill me, I have to build a somewhat efficent killer.<br /> I will have high melee, and will be sporting the five point artifact sword Soul Mirror (since it's decent as is AND I can boost it and go boss mode).<br /> I will have kinda high sailing, since I will be our groups &quot;cab&quot;. My deathlord will provide me with the Folding ship.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you as a group discussed the concept of PvP rather than PvE play? Because you seem to be creating a stealth adverserial character and then deciding that if you get found out as playing a concept which has gone against group think you need to be in a place where you can kill the other players?<br /> <br /> Depending on group this could be seen as great fun, or spoiling everyone else's stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1181-molez","name":"Molez","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T09:46:18-08:00","id":426644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/424557-wolf-amongst-sheep-playing-an-abyssal-posing-as-a-solar?p=426633#post426633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's <i>that</i> got to do with the morality of using soulsteel? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>What did you think happened to the complainers? Gotta have *some* ready for the deluxe Abyssal KS.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:White\">Doubting the relevance, since both Abyssals and Exigents-that-can-be-mocked-up-into-Abyssals are like a year away; either the OP's group doesn't ditch his PC for the sake of Ex3, in which case the proximity of Ex3 (and thus your post) is irrelevant, <b>or</b> the OP's group ditches his PC for the sake of Ex3, in which case this whole thread (and thus your post) is irrelevant.</span> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't seem like a particularly big deal to play a 3e solar and call it an abyssal in the mean time, using any differences we get given in Antagonists. Frankly it wouldn't be much different to playing a 2e Abyssal anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1414-pyrosorc","name":"Pyrosorc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T11:25:44-08:00","id":426729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/424557-wolf-amongst-sheep-playing-an-abyssal-posing-as-a-solar?p=425577#post425577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then <i>you're</i> the one <i>destroying souls</i>.<br /> That's like going to a maximum-security prison and murdering all the death-row inmates.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean realistically in Creation who fucking cares.<br /> <br /> It's not like Creation is gonna run outta souls - it manufactures its own. The loss of a soul is an abstract loss in Creation - it doesn't really affect anything but the soul in question.<br /> <br /> Fuck your victims' souls. If they were stronger, maybe they wouldn't have lost. It's their fault for being so weak.<br /> <br /> <i>Vae victus.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T13:07:45-08:00","id":426905,"title":"","content":"Can you feed soulsteel to a rhaksha? I know they eat parts of a persons spiritual self and stuff in 2nd and there is the idea presented in their splat book that rhaksha will occasionally devour people who get unmade by the wyld, but can that apply to soulsteel? Just thinking it would make for amusing negotiations if the rhaksha insisted on trying to eat an abyssal's equipment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T13:19:45-08:00","id":426919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/424557-wolf-amongst-sheep-playing-an-abyssal-posing-as-a-solar?p=426905#post426905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you feed soulsteel to a rhaksha? I know they eat parts of a persons spiritual self and stuff in 2nd and there is the idea presented in their splat book that rhaksha will occasionally devour people who get unmade by the wyld, but can that apply to soulsteel? Just thinking it would make for amusing negotiations if the rhaksha insisted on trying to eat an abyssal's equipment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not, in the same way that olive oil that has been burned can no longer be used for cooking. Sure, it's still <i>around</i>, but not in a consumable form.<br /> <br /> Although in th Wyld, anything goes - the sword might get unmade into delicious bacon strips that taste like Valor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T13:54:18-08:00","id":426966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Molez</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/424557-wolf-amongst-sheep-playing-an-abyssal-posing-as-a-solar?p=426637#post426637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have you as a group discussed the concept of PvP rather than PvE play? Because you seem to be creating a stealth adverserial character and then deciding that if you get found out as playing a concept which has gone against group think you need to be in a place where you can kill the other players?<br /> <br /> Depending on group this could be seen as great fun, or spoiling everyone else's stories.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Unsuspected stealthkills on PCs are probably NOT gonna go down well, but that is not my plan.<br /> My degree of stealthiness will more be about the disguise and just a small touch of stealth. Hopefully I wont have to go PVP before I get abyssal version of fivefold bulward stance. If I get there I just have to add an armour to that, and I think I can be a serious threat without doing stealthkills. IF (and that's a big if) I'm gonna kill them from stealth, they are atleast gonna know they are being hunted.<br /> It will all depend on when, where and IF they found my nature. If they found it out without me noticing I'm gonna be in deep fecal matter, but if they don't and I can plan the showdown, and maybe get a few dangerous ghosts to fight alongside me, THEY are gonna find themselves upp feces creek without a artifact foldingship<br /> I'm gonna have to be able to wing it, and as I see it my job is<br /> 1) have fun the entire time myself<br /> 2) create fun for the rest of the party, up to and including a climactic fight scene.<br /> It is NOT to win and cause a TPK... but as Ivan Drago said. If he die, he dies.<br /> <br /> But hey, maybe I will grow to like my party and grow enough balls to throw of the chains of my liege.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4872-evilof","name":"evilof","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}